ss":"beating"},{"surface":"அணிகொள்","parts":[{"text":"அணி","lemma":"அணி","gloss":"beauty"},{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"தேர்வழி","parts":[{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"தேர்","gloss":"chariot"},{"text":"வழி","lemma":"வழி","gloss":"path"}],"gloss":"path of chariots"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடுங்கண்","parts":[{"text":"கடும்","lemma":"கடும்","gloss":"fierce"},{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"valor"}],"gloss":"fierce valor"},{"surface":"பருகுநர்","parts":[{"text":"பருகு","lemma":"பருகு","gloss":"drink"},{"text":"நர்","lemma":"நர்","gloss":"those who"}],"gloss":"those who drink"},{"surface":"நடுங்குகை","parts":[{"text":"நடுங்கு","lemma":"நடுங்கு","gloss":"tremble"},{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand"}],"gloss":"trembling hands"},{"surface":"உகத்த","parts":[{"text":"உகத்த","lemma":"உகத்த","gloss":"which spilled"}],"gloss":"which spilled","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நறுஞ்சேறு","parts":[{"text":"நறுஞ்சேறு","lemma":"நறுஞ்சேறு","gloss":"fragrant paste"}],"gloss":"fragrant paste","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆடிய","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"ஆடு","gloss":"bathe"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past participle"}],"gloss":"which bathed in"},{"surface":"வறுந்தலை","parts":[{"text":"வறும்","lemma":"வறும்","gloss":"empty"},{"text":"தலை","lemma":"தலை","gloss":"head"}],"gloss":"empty-headed"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephants"}],"gloss":"elephants"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெடுனகர்","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"நெடு","gloss":"tall"},{"text":"னகர்","lemma":"னகர்","gloss":"palace"}],"gloss":"tall palace"},{"surface":"வரைப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"வரைப்பு","lemma":"வரைப்பு","gloss":"courtyard"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the courtyard"},{"surface":"படுமுழா","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"படு","gloss":"sounding"},{"text":"முழா","lemma":"முழா","gloss":"drum"}],"gloss":"sounding drums"},{"surface":"ஓர்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"listen"},{"text":"க்கும்","lemma":"க்கும்","gloss":"habitual participle"}],"gloss":"listening to"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உறந்தையோனே","parts":[{"text":"உறந்தை","lemma":"உறந்தை","gloss":"Uraiyur"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ஓன்","gloss":"he of"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"he of Uraiyur"},{"surface":"குருசில்","parts":[{"text":"குருசில்","lemma":"குருசில்","gloss":"O lord"}],"gloss":"O lord!"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிறன்கடை","parts":[{"text":"பிறன்","lemma":"பிறன்","gloss":"other's"},{"text":"கடை","lemma":"கடை","gloss":"gate"}],"gloss":"others' gates"},{"surface":"மறப்ப","parts":[{"text":"மற","lemma":"மற","gloss":"forget"},{"text":"ப","lemma":"ப","gloss":"infinitive"}],"gloss":"to forget"},{"surface":"நல்குவன்","parts":[{"text":"நல்குவன்","lemma":"நல்குவன்","gloss":"he will bestow"}],"gloss":"he will bestow","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செலினே","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"செல்","gloss":"go"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"if"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"if you go"}]}],"literal":"Like the peeled skin of an iguana, on the side where bones protrude, / not seeing anyone to remove the intense hunger of your family, / grieving and grieving over the learning that has fallen on deaf ears, / what do you do here, O bard, bearing ornaments? / On his chest with beautiful, majestic, red spots, / bowing to women with gentleness, and with strength / binding men, the great noble man of great pride, / like the breast dripping milk for a newborn infant, / the Kaveri river which flowed with tree-destroying abundant water, / the king of the good country that protects mankind, / since internal enmity has settled on one side, to the enmity of birds / he does not heed, saying 'we will die', / unyielding warriors striking their strong shoulders, / where war drums are beaten on the path of beautiful chariots, / where those who drink with fierce valor spilled from trembling hands, / elephants with empty heads that bathed in fragrant paste, / listening to the sounding drums in the courtyard of the tall palace, / he of Uraiyur, O lord! / If you go to him, he will bestow gifts so that you forget the gates of others.","translation":"O bard! With bones protruding on your sides like the peeled skin of an iguana, not finding anyone to relieve the intense hunger of your family, and grieving deeply that your learning has fallen on deaf ears, what are you doing here, bearing empty ornaments? Go to the lord of Uraiyur! On his chest, adorned with beautiful, majestic red spots, he bows with gentleness to women, yet binds men with his strength. He is the great noble king of the fertile land nourished by the Kaveri, whose abundant, tree-sweeping waters flow like milk from a mother's breast to her newborn infant. In his city, since internal enemies have been subdued, his unyielding warriors, declaring they would rather die than heed bad omens, strike their strong shoulders as war drums beat along the path of beautiful chariots. There, elephants with unarmored heads, bathed in fragrant paste, listen to the sounding drums in the courtyard of his tall palace, while those who drink with fierce valor spill toddy from their trembling hands. If you go to him, O lord, he will bestow such wealth upon you that you will forever forget the gates of other patrons.","modern":"உரித்த உடும்பின் தோல் போல விலா எலும்புகள் வெளியே தெரியும்படி, உமது சுற்றத்தாரின் கொடிய பசியைப் போக்க வல்லவரைக் காணாமல், செவிசாய்க்காதவர்களிடம் உமது கல்வியைக் கூறி நொந்து நொந்து, வறுமையிலும் அணிகலன்களைச் சுமந்து கொண்டு இங்கு என்ன செய்கிறாய் பாணனே? பெண்களுக்கு மென்மையுடன் பணிந்து, ஆண்களைத் தன் வலிமையால் பிணிக்கும் பெருமை பொருந்திய நெஞ்சினைக் கொண்டவன், சோழன் நலங்கிள்ளி. தன் தாயின் முலைப்பால் பச்சிளம் குழந்தைக்குச் சுரப்பது போல, மரங்களை அடித்துச் செல்லும் காவிரி நீர் பாயும் வளநாட்டைக் காக்கும் தலைவன் அவன். அவனுடைய உறையூரில், உட்பகைகள் ஒழிந்துவிட்டதால், சகுனப் பறவைகளின் தீய நிமித்தங்களை மதியாமல், 'போரின்றி வீணாகச் சாவோம்' என்று கூறி, மறவர்கள் தங்கள் தோள்களைத் தட்டி ஆரவாரம் செய்கிறார்கள். தேர்கள் செல்லும் வழியில் முரசுகள் முழங்குகின்றன. வீரர்கள் கள் பருகி நடுங்கும் கைகளால் சிந்திய நறுமணச் சேற்றில் யானைகள் விளையாடுகின்றன. அத்தகைய உயர்ந்த அரண்மனையில் முழவு ஒலிகள் கேட்கின்றன. அங்குள்ள உறையூர் தலைவனிடம் நீ சென்றால், பிற வள்ளல்களின் வாசல்களை நீ மறக்கும்படி அவன் உனக்குப் பெருஞ்செல்வத்தை வாரி வழங்குவான்.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Kovur Kizhar addresses a poor bard who is suffering from extreme poverty. The poet describes the bard's ribs protruding like the peeled skin of an iguana, symbolizing his starvation, and his grief over his art being ignored by unappreciative patrons. He directs the bard to Cholan Nalangilli of Uraiyur, describing the king's immense generosity, which is compared to a mother's milk flowing for her newborn. The poem also highlights the prosperity and martial pride of the Chola kingdom, where warriors are eager for battle and ignore bad omens because internal enemies are already subdued. The key words include 'உடும்பு உரித்து அன்ன' (like peeled iguana skin), 'சுரந்த காவிரி' (the flowing Kaveri), and 'உறந்தையோனே' (he of Uraiyur).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.1],[2.1,3.4],[3.4,3.8],[3.8,4.2],[4.2,4.9],[5.1,6.1],[6.1,6.6],[6.6,6.9],[6.9,7.1],[7.1,7.5],[7.74,9.0],[9.0,9.5],[9.5,9.7],[9.7,10.2],[10.2,10.67],[10.67,11.6],[11.6,12.2],[12.2,12.4],[12.4,12.6],[12.6,12.7],[12.7,14.3],[14.3,14.9],[14.9,15.2],[15.2,15.8],[15.8,16.7],[16.7,17.1],[17.1,17.2],[17.2,17.7],[17.7,19.0],[19.0,19.3],[19.3,19.4],[19.4,20.6],[20.6,20.9],[21.64,22.24],[22.24,22.44],[22.44,22.74],[22.74,23.14],[23.14,24.54],[24.54,24.74],[24.74,25.24],[25.24,25.84],[25.84,26.94],[26.94,27.04],[27.04,27.84],[27.84,28.74],[28.74,29.54],[29.54,29.64],[29.64,30.14],[30.14,30.64],[30.64,30.84],[30.84,31.84],[31.84,32.14],[32.14,32.84],[32.84,33.32],[33.51,34.24],[34.24,34.74],[34.74,34.94],[34.94,35.97],[35.97,35.97],[35.97